    "created_at": "2026-03-13T20:35:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-13T20:35:54Z",
    "body": "I like the direction of providing a native element for this pattern instead of requiring `role=\"toolbar\"` and custom keyboard logic.\n\nA few questions:\n\n- Would the keyboard navigation follow the same interaction model defined for toolbars in [WAI-ARIA](https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/toolbar/examples/toolbar/) (arrow key navigation between controls)?\n- Would orientation be configurable (similar to `aria-orientation`)?\n- If `focusgroups` do not end up being standardized, would the keyboard behavior still be defined directly on `<toolbar>`?\n- This seems especially useful for rich editors and web apps where implementing consistent toolbar focus management today requires quite a bit of custom JS.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/4057852548/reactions",
