    "created_at": "2026-03-13T23:11:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-13T23:11:38Z",
    "body": "Responses:\n\n1. Yes the idea is that the toolbar will automatically collapse its focusable children into a single tab stop with arrow keys to navigate between them.\n\n2. This is still an open question, but yes it seems likely we'll provide an orientation attribute that updates aria-orientation, the set of keyboard arrows that work and the default styling of the element.\n\n3. Yes, if focusgroup as an attribute doesn't end up in the standard the idea is that the keyboard logic would be copied from that PR and applied directly to toolbar. Lots of thought went into the key conflict handling and it's particularly useful for the toolbar pattern.\n\n4. Yes, I agree, the status quo requires a lot of non-trivial JS to get right and providing this built-in would help ensure consistency and make it easier to implement these patterns correctly.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
